  <dataqual>
    <attracc>
      <attraccr>Data was inspected to ensure that "Buff_Dist" value equals the width of the buffer in feet on each side of the boundary.  At this time, all buffers are 20 feet.</attraccr>
    </attracc>
    <logic>Checks were conducted to ensure that the buffer was applied to the polygons appropriately and that the distance on the ground generally measured 20 feet on either side of the CBRS boundary.</logic>
    <complete>This buffer polygon data set has been checked to ensure that all external CBRS boundaries over land are covered by the appropriate buffer width. Coincident boundaries that are shared by two units or between prohibition areas (depicted in CBRS_Prohibitions) were not buffered. The seaward side of a CBRS unit is generally defined by either the 20-foot or the 30-foot bathymetric contour (depending on the location of the unit) and is usually unmapped. Because of this, seaward boundaries that are based on the location of a bathymetric contour are not covered by a buffer polygon in this data set. For more information on seaward CBRS boundaries see the metadata for the “CBRS Polygons” and “CBRS Prohibitions” data sets. The metadata is available at https://www.fws.gov/media/digital-coastal-barrier-resources-system-boundaries.</complete>
    <posacc>
      <horizpa>
        <horizpar>This horizontal accuracy buffer dataset is intended to convey the horizontal positional accuracy of the “CBRS Polygons” and “CBRS Prohibitions” data sets. Thus, an accuracy assessment of the horizontal positional information is not applicable. For more information on the horizontal positional accuracy of the associated “CBRS Polygons” and “CBRS Prohibitions” data sets, see the metadata. The metadata is available at https://www.fws.gov/media/digital-coastal-barrier-resources-system-boundaries.</horizpar>
      </horizpa>
      <vertacc>
        <vertaccr>A formal accuracy assessment of the vertical positional information in the data is not applicable.</vertaccr>
      </vertacc>
    </posacc>
